{"route":"/docs/6.0/customize/transitions/","version":"6.0","renderedVersion":"6.0","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Transitions","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Learn how Bootstrap components animate, which state classes drive them, and how to retune or remove the motion."},"blocks":[{"id":"how-it-works","type":"heading","en":"How it works","level":2},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"CSS owns every component transition in Bootstrap. JavaScript only toggles a state class and then waits for the transition to finish before it fires an event or removes an element."},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"This means you restyle motion with CSS alone. You never have to reimplement a component to change how it animates."},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Each animated component follows the same three rules:"},{"id":"how-it-works--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ol","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"how-it-works--item-1","type":"item","en":"The base selector holds the hidden state, plus the <code>transition</code> declaration."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"how-it-works--item-2","type":"item","en":"A state class holds the visible state."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"how-it-works--item-3","type":"item","en":"<code>@starting-style</code> supplies the enter-from state, because the element is not rendered before the state class lands."}]}]},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"The toast is the reference implementation."},{"id":"how-it-works--code-1","type":"code","value":"// Animated variant (default). `display` transitions discretely so the toast\n// stays laid out until the fade-out finishes. Add .toast-instant to skip it.\n&:not(.toast-instant) {\n  opacity: 0;\n  @include transition-props(\n    var(--toast-transition-property),\n    var(--toast-transition-duration),\n    var(--toast-transition-timing),\n    allow-discrete\n  );\n}\n\n&.show {\n  display: flex;\n  opacity: 1;\n}","language":""},{"id":"how-it-works--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>display</code> transitions with <code>allow-discrete</code> so the toast stays laid out until the fade-out ends. Without it, the element would disappear on the first frame and you would see no exit animation."},{"id":"state-classes","type":"heading","en":"State classes","level":2},{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"JavaScript adds and removes a small, fixed set of classes. Style these, and your customizations follow the component."},{"id":"state-classes--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Class"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Meaning"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>.show</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"The component is shown. Its absence is the hidden state. Used by collapse, menu, popover, toast, and tooltip. Collapse toggles nothing else."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>.active</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"The shown state for tab panes, where it also marks the selected pane."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>.hiding</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"Present only while an exit transition plays. Bootstrap removes it after the transition ends. Used by alert, dialog, and drawer."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>.{component}-instant</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-11","type":"paragraph","en":"Opts one element out of its transition, such as <code>.toast-instant</code> or <code>.dialog-instant</code>."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-12","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>.{component}-static</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-13","type":"paragraph","en":"A short bounce that signals a modal refused to close, such as <code>.dialog-static</code>."}]}]}]},{"id":"state-classes--paragraph-14","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>.hiding</code> exists for components that must survive their own exit. An alert is removed from the DOM and a dialog leaves the top layer, so both need a class that marks the outgoing state. Components that only hide can drop <code>.show</code> instead."},{"id":"customize-the-motion","type":"heading","en":"Customize the motion","level":2},{"id":"token-trio","type":"heading","en":"Token trio","level":3},{"id":"token-trio--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Every animated component exposes the same three custom properties."},{"id":"token-trio--table-1","type":"table","caption":[],"rows":[{"head":true,"cells":[{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"token-trio--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Custom property"}]},{"type":"th","body":[{"id":"token-trio--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Purpose"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"token-trio--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>--bs-{component}-transition-property</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"token-trio--paragraph-5","type":"paragraph","en":"The properties that animate."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"token-trio--paragraph-6","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>--bs-{component}-transition-duration</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"token-trio--paragraph-7","type":"paragraph","en":"How long the animation runs. Set it to <code>0s</code> to remove the motion."}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"token-trio--paragraph-8","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>--bs-{component}-transition-timing</code>"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"token-trio--paragraph-9","type":"paragraph","en":"The easing curve."}]}]}]},{"id":"token-trio--paragraph-10","type":"paragraph","en":"Because the property list is a token, you can animate something new without rewriting the whole declaration. Add <code>transform</code> to the toast list, and the toast slides as it fades. Press the button to replay it."},{"id":"token-trio--example-1","type":"demo","key":"8cd8f116b041d0a326c4","height":174,"anchors":["slideToast","slideToastBtn"]},{"id":"token-trio--code-1","type":"code","value":".toast-slide {\n  --bs-toast-transition-property: opacity, transform, display;\n  --bs-toast-transition-duration: .3s;\n  --bs-toast-transition-timing: ease-out;\n\n  transform: translateY(1rem);\n}\n\n.toast-slide.show {\n  transform: none;\n}","language":""},{"id":"token-trio--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"token-trio--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"Keep the discrete property in the list. The toast and the menu need <code>display</code>, and the dialog and the drawer need <code>visibility</code>. That property is what keeps the element rendered until the exit animation ends."}]},{"id":"size-animations","type":"heading","en":"Size animations","level":3},{"id":"size-animations--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Collapse and accordion animate a size, not an opacity, so they add <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/interpolate-size\"><code>interpolate-size</code></a> to let <code>0</code> interpolate to the <code>auto</code> of the open state. No JavaScript measures the content. Browsers without <code>interpolate-size</code> open and close the element at once, which is why the collapse clips the animated axis at all times."},{"id":"size-animations--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"The collapse trio carries the component name last, because the two components share it."},{"id":"size-animations--code-1","type":"code","value":"// stylelint-disable custom-property-no-missing-var-function\n$collapse-tokens: defaults(\n  (\n    --transition-collapse-property: \"block-size, display\",\n    --transition-collapse-duration: .35s,\n    --transition-collapse-timing: ease,\n  ),\n  $collapse-tokens\n);\n// stylelint-enable custom-property-no-missing-var-function","language":""},{"id":"shared-easing","type":"heading","en":"Shared easing","level":3},{"id":"shared-easing--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Dialog, drawer, and menu read one easing curve from <code>:root</code>, so a single override restyles all three overlays."},{"id":"shared-easing--code-1","type":"code","value":"// Shared easing curve for overlay components (dialog, drawer, menu)\n--transition-timing-overlay: cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1),","language":""},{"id":"remove-the-motion","type":"heading","en":"Remove the motion","level":2},{"id":"remove-the-motion--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"You have four options, from the narrowest to the widest:"},{"id":"remove-the-motion--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ol","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"remove-the-motion--item-1","type":"item","en":"Add the component&#39;s <code>-instant</code> class to one element, such as <code>.toast-instant</code>."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"remove-the-motion--item-2","type":"item","en":"Add the <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/motion\"><code>.transition-none</code> utility</a> to one element."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"remove-the-motion--item-3","type":"item","en":"Set a <code>-duration</code> token to <code>0s</code> for a component or a subtree."}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"remove-the-motion--item-4","type":"item","en":"Set the <code>$enable-transitions</code> Sass option to <code>false</code> to remove all transitions at build time."}]}]},{"id":"remove-the-motion--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap wraps its transitions in <code>prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference</code>, so users who ask for less motion already get instant state changes. See <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/accessibility#reduced-motion\">reduced motion</a> for more."},{"id":"remove-the-motion--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"JavaScript reads the computed transition duration before it waits. When the duration is <code>0s</code>, events and promises resolve immediately, whatever removed the motion."},{"id":"events-and-promises","type":"heading","en":"Events and promises","level":2},{"id":"events-and-promises--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>show()</code> and <code>hide()</code> return promises that resolve after the transition ends. The matching <code>shown</code> and <code>hidden</code> events fire at the same time."},{"id":"events-and-promises--code-1","type":"code","value":"const toast = new bootstrap.Toast('#myToast')\n\nawait toast.show()\n// The fade-in has finished.","language":""},{"id":"events-and-promises--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"An element with no transition still resolves, just on the next tick."}],"demos":[{"key":"8cd8f116b041d0a326c4","html":"<div class=\"toast-container position-static\"><div class=\"toast bd-toast-slide\" id=\"slideToast\" role=\"alert\" aria-live=\"assertive\" aria-atomic=\"true\"><div class=\"toast-body\"><p>This toast slides up as it fades in.</p></div></div></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn-solid theme-primary mt-3\" id=\"slideToastBtn\">Replay</button>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""}],"nav":[{"en":"Install","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/install"},{"en":"AI","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/ai"},{"en":"Approach","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/approach"},{"en":"CSS variables","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getting-started/css-variables"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/getti